{"name":"Green Snow","hex":"#9eb788","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green snow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Snow that is colored green by the growth of microscopic algae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green_snow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snow","blocks":[{"text":"Snow is a form of solid atmospheric precipitation consisting of individual ice crystals that grow while suspended in the air—usually within clouds—and then fall, accumulating on the ground, where they undergo further changes. It consists of frozen crystalline water throughout its life cycle, starting when, under suitable conditions, the ice crystals form in the atmosphere, increase to millimeter size, precipitate and accumulate on surfaces, then metamorphose in place, and ultimately melt, slide, or sublimate away."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg/330px-CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow","wikidata":"Q7561"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg/500px-CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg/1280px-CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg/500px-CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Feb242007_blizzard.gif/500px-Feb242007_blizzard.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Feb242007_blizzard.gif/1280px-Feb242007_blizzard.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Feb242007_blizzard.gif/500px-Feb242007_blizzard.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Extratropical cyclonic snowstorm, February 24, 2007—(Click for animation.)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFeb242007_blizzard.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common